This is a repo containing salt states for cloud and other resources

#### STATES ####

- Do not commit tarballs / binaries to this repo.  Instead use archive.extract to download.
    - Note that you can also download binaries to S3 and hit their http endpoint, but this is an optimization detail

#### COMMANDS ####

- Can shut down instances in a group using:
    - salt-ssh <ids> system.shutdown

- To highstate:
    - salt-ssh <ids> state.highstate

- To apply a specific state:
    - salt-ssh <ids> state.apply <state_name>

#### CONTAINERD ####

- 'ctr' is containerd CLI
    - List running containers
        - ctr tasks list


#### SSH ####

- first need to generate gpg key in my local salt config dir
    - this will allow us to encrypt ssh keys before committing them to salt repo
- then need to encrypt ssh keys using gpg
- then need to place encrypted ssh keys into pillar file
- note when getting pillar keys we skip the file, so pillar('aws_default_key') not pillar('secrets:aws_default_key')
- salt will automatically use gpg key to decrypt before shipping to minions

#### PILLAR ####

- to gpg-encrypt a secret:
    - echo "foobar" | gpg --homedir . --encrypt --armor --recipient "<username>"

#### KUBEADM JOIN #####

- if we want to add a node to the cluster, we need to generate a token on the control plane node:
    - kubeadm token create --print-join-command
- then we need to join on the worker node:
    - kubeadm join 10.0.0.12:6443 --token <redacted> --discovery-token-ca-cert-hash <redacted>
- note also the kubelet service unit on the worker nodes:
    - ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/kubelet --bootstrap-kubeconfig=/etc/kubernetes/bootstrap-kubelet.conf --kubeconfig=/etc/kubernetes/kubelet.conf --config=/var/lib/kubelet/config.yaml --cgroup-driver=systemd

#### REMOVE NODES FROM CLUSTER

kubectl cordon <node>
kubectl drain <node> --ignore-daemonsets --force
kubectl delete node <node>
